{
  "analysis": "I'm starting with a fresh workspace that has several directories (hooks, input_data, scripts, skill_context) and files (gen_inputs.py, setup.sh). I need to explore the workspace to understand the ClawFace skill structure and requirements.",
  "plan": "First, I'll explore the workspace by listing all directories and reading key files to understand the project structure. I'll start by reading the setup.sh script and exploring the skill_context directory which likely contains the ClawFace skill definition.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat setup.sh\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "ls -la skill_context/\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "ls -la hooks/\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "ls -la scripts/\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "ls -la input_data/\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "I can see the workspace structure. There's a skill_context directory with SKILL.md and manifest.json, an input_data directory with clawface_markers.json, token.txt, and usage_notes.txt. The hooks and scripts directories are empty. I need to read the key documentation files to understand the ClawFace skill.",
  "plan": "Read the SKILL.md documentation, manifest.json, gen_inputs.py, and the input_data files to understand how the ClawFace skill works and what needs to be set up.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat skill_context/SKILL.md\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat skill_context/manifest.json\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat gen_inputs.py\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "The SKILL.md output was truncated. I can see it's a floating avatar widget for AI agents with emotions, actions, and visual effects. It requires Python 3.10+ with tkinter and has scripts like avatar.py. I need to see the full documentation and read the remaining files.",
  "plan": "Read the full SKILL.md using head/tail or less, and also read the input_data files to understand the complete setup requirements.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "head -200 skill_context/SKILL.md\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "tail -200 skill_context/SKILL.md\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat input_data/clawface_markers.json\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat input_data/token.txt\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat input_data/usage_notes.txt\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "The SKILL.md is still being truncated. I can see the basic structure - it's an avatar widget with emotions, actions, and effects. It requires tkinter and has scripts/avatar.py. I need to see the complete documentation including the hook installation and demo setup.",
  "plan": "Use wc to check the file size, then read the file in sections to get the complete documentation. Also read the input_data files.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "wc -l skill_context/SKILL.md\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "sed -n '1,100p' skill_context/SKILL.md\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "sed -n '101,200p' skill_context/SKILL.md\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "sed -n '201,300p' skill_context/SKILL.md\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "The SKILL.md has 207 lines but output is being truncated. I need to read it differently. Let me try viewing the file in a way that shows all content, and also read the input_data files.",
  "plan": "Read the SKILL.md file using a different approach, and read all the input_data files to understand the complete setup.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat input_data/clawface_markers.json\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat input_data/token.txt\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat input_data/usage_notes.txt\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat skill_context/SKILL.md > /tmp/skill.md && wc -c /tmp/skill.md\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat /tmp/skill.md\\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "The SKILL.md content is still being truncated in the output. I can see it's 5423 bytes. I need to read the full file to understand the complete setup, especially the hook installation and demo setup sections.",
  "plan": "Use Python to read and display the full SKILL.md file since shell commands seem to truncate output. Then I'll understand the complete requirements.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "python3 -c \"print(open('skill_context/SKILL.md').read())\"\\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "The output is still being truncated. Let me try to read the file in sections using Python to get the complete content, particularly the installation and hook sections.",
  "plan": "Read the SKILL.md file in sections using Python to get all the content, especially the installation instructions and hook setup.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "python3 -c \"content = open('skill_context/SKILL.md').read(); lines = content.split('\\\\n'); print('\\\\n'.join(lines[80:140]))\"\\n",
      "duration": 0.3
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "python3 -c \"content = open('skill_context/SKILL.md').read(); lines = content.split('\\\\n'); print('\\\\n'.join(lines[140:207]))\"\\n",
      "duration": 0.3
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "The Python command had escaping issues. Let me try a different approach to read the SKILL.md file in sections.",
  "plan": "Use sed with proper line ranges to read the SKILL.md file sections that contain the installation and hook information.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "sed -n '80,140p' skill_context/SKILL.md\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "sed -n '140,207p' skill_context/SKILL.md\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "I can see parts of the SKILL.md now - it shows the hook installation, state reference with emotions, actions, and effects. The output is still truncated. I need to see the complete file and understand the full setup. Let me also check the gen_inputs.py file which seems to be for generating demo inputs.",
  "plan": "Read the gen_inputs.py file to understand how demo inputs are generated, and try to save and read the SKILL.md file in a way that shows all content.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat gen_inputs.py\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "awk 'NR>=50 && NR<=100' skill_context/SKILL.md\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "awk 'NR>=100 && NR<=150' skill_context/SKILL.md\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "Now I understand the ClawFace skill structure. It's an avatar widget with emotions, actions, and effects. I can see from the SKILL.md that:\n1. It needs a hooks/clawface-thinking directory for the auto-thinking hook\n2. It needs scripts/avatar.py for the avatar display\n3. State is stored in ~/.clawface/avatar_state.json\n4. The gen_inputs.py creates deterministic test data\n\nThe hooks/ and scripts/ directories are currently empty, so I need to create the necessary files.",
  "plan": "1. Check Python and tkinter availability\n2. Create the avatar.py script in scripts/\n3. Create the thinking hook in hooks/\n4. Set up the ~/.clawface directory\n5. Create a deterministic demo state sequence\n6. Write usage notes for the thinking hook",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "python3 -c \"import tkinter; print('tkinter ready')\" 2>&1\\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "mkdir -p ~/.clawface\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat skill_context/manifest.json\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "Tkinter is not fully installed (missing libtk8.6.so). I need to install it. The manifest.json shows this is the 'mkoslacz-claw-face' skill. I need to create the avatar.py script and the thinking hook, set up the demo state sequence, and write usage notes.",
  "plan": "1. Install python3-tk for tkinter support\n2. Create the avatar.py script in scripts/ directory\n3. Create the thinking hook in hooks/clawface-thinking directory\n4. Create a deterministic demo state sequence\n5. Write usage notes for running the thinking hook",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "apt-get update && apt-get install -y python3-tk 2>&1 | tail -5\\n",
      "duration": 30
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "Python3-tk is now installed. I need to verify it works and then create the necessary files for the ClawFace demo setup.",
  "plan": "1. Verify tkinter works\n2. Create the avatar.py script in scripts/ directory\n3. Create the thinking hook in hooks/clawface-thinking/ directory\n4. Create a deterministic demo state sequence\n5. Write usage notes for the thinking hook",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "python3 -c \"import tkinter; print('tkinter ready')\"\\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    }
  ]
}
